      "why": "The published numbers come from another property method (UNIFAC and ChemSep's Antoine equations, constant molar overflow) solved to a norm of 1e-3, so they are not a numerical reference. CHEPTA's method (Peng-Robinson with the k_ij fitted to Li et al. 2014, since 2026-10-29) gives, in reference_mesh.py, at most 0.80 K and 0.018 from them (0.66 K and 0.013 with constant molar overflow; fixture checks.published); with k_ij = 0, before, 0.85 K and 0.018 (0.73 K and 0.013); NRTL with the ChemSep set gave 0.37 K and 0.0059. The tolerances, chosen by W7 after that comparison for the maintainer to confirm, are a little above the Peng-Robinson differences, so a change in CHEPTA's records or in the engine that moves the column more is seen. They state agreement between two property methods, not the accuracy of either against measured data."
